 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Everyone starts somewhere. Would you rather start with basic drawing exercises, or something you' love to draw, like people, animals, or landscapes? Start with simple lines. A pencil and a piece of paper are all you need. Draw a grid of squares on your page, then fill one box with straight lines. It' about control. The grid gives you a frame of reference, so you can focus on the lines themselves, rather than the overall picture. That's a great start. Your stick people are yours, and you can build on that.",
